{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1559130-need-help-with-trying-to-have-a-place-for-both-the-inferno-and-princess-s-dark-world","id":1559130,"title":"Need help with trying to have a place for both the Inferno and Princess's Dark World","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-03-30T19:56:35-07:00","id":1559130,"title":"Need help with trying to have a place for both the Inferno and Princess's Dark World","content":"Any suggestions. This is just for my personal setting","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24310-metrere-oil","name":"Metrere Oil","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-30T20:44:59-07:00","id":1559131,"title":"","content":"Could you clarify what you mean by &quot;have a place for both&quot; in this context? Setting aside minor differences in presentation of the Dark World between versions of Princess, the Inferno is fairly distinct in the way it and its denizens work in contrast to most forms of Darkspawn et al.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-30T20:59:30-07:00","id":1559132,"title":"","content":"I realize that that they both work differently. It's more about the stuff that drives them, since there is quite a lot of overlap. The Inferno being about destructive transgression and the Darkness being about malice, despair and self-loathing.<br /> <br /> I suppose one difference I can maybe see is the Inferno caring more for the effects and harm done, whilst the Dark, if I remember is more tied to the emotions driving the actions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24310-metrere-oil","name":"Metrere Oil","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-31T07:31:05-07:00","id":1559142,"title":"","content":"My only idea relies on motivation that each category of creature could have:<br /> <br /> Devils <i>want</i>. They have &quot;constructive&quot; desires that feed and empower them, even if as they make the world a worse place. They enjoy their corrupting actions, too.<br /> <br /> Darkspawn <i>suffer</i>. Their nature locks them in an existence of endless suffering, and all they can do is lash out. Whatever harm they do won't ever make them feel better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-31T18:39:02-07:00","id":1559151,"title":"","content":"Speaking with more confidence on the matter of devils than on Darkspawn, the denizens of the Inferno are bent toward the goals of eroding human empathy and morality, whether directly through temptation or indirectly through making people think the life and the world aren't worth respecting because life is cheap and the world is corrupt and defiled; Nemeses somewhat break this pattern by punishing sin, but even that fits into the bigger picture by a) taking sinners off the board soon enough to keep from killing the golden goose and b) floating the peripheral temptation for prospective infernalists to think they can get away with it by establishing that messing with devils comes with consequences to evade.<br /> <br /> I guess another point of emphasis in difference is that the Inferno is actively uncomfortable to be in at best, pushing its denizens and prisoners to move toward temptation or away from torment, whereas the Dark World's default state outside of Taints and other zones of activity is more void-coded \u2014 cold and dark and everything is dead-or-close-enough.<br /> <br /> The Inferno is desire. The Dark World is depression.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-06T14:26:48-07:00","id":1559255,"title":"","content":"Are you familiar with the other so called &quot;lower depths&quot;? I'm not that familiar with Princess but there is certainly room in the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-16T04:45:17-07:00","id":1559448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I realize that that they both work differently. It's more about the stuff that drives them, since there is quite a lot of overlap </div> </div> </div>The Outer Dark is for the most part reductive. You create a Darkspawn by removing every part of a person that's not Darkspawn, with the addition of magical stuff called &quot;Taint&quot;/&quot;Darkness&quot; to fill the gaps.<br /> <br /> The Inferno. Satan may be a lesser being than he was as god's brightest angel but in many portrayals, especially urban fantasy as opposed to theology, he's more than a man. More powerful, more knowledgeable, more cunning, and more cosmically significant. The closest thing to god's opposite. <br /> <br /> So I'd lean into that if you want to differentiate them. Joining the Inferno requires achieving your ambitions (or the tempting whisper in your head achieving <i>its</i> ambitions), growing into a powerful, cunning, demonic creature. Someone who matters in the secret games played behind the scenes. Where as joining the Darkness can happen accidentality, and so easily that particularly bad outbreaks of the Darkness spread like zombie apocalypses. But it turns you into little more than a miserable wretch of an animal. (There are smarter dark creatures who hunt via cunning, tempting etc, but as a rule they're not great at it. Infernal demons are very good at what they do).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}